{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>For every shepherd is an abomination to the Egyptians etc.</b> Shepherds were abhorrent in their eyes, for sheep was an abhorrent thing to eat, just as goats are abhorrent for eating in many places. And likewise, ״they may not eat bread with the Hebrews״ — for it is an abomination to the Egyptians: the people of עבר הנהר were abhorrent in their eyes, and therefore it was hard for them to eat with them. And likewise, ״we shall sacrifice the abomination of the Egyptians before their eyes״ — we slaughter before them that which is abhorrent to them — ״and will they not stone us״: they will kill us. It does not say יהרגונו but rather יסקלונו. Another interpretation: I heard, ״the abomination of the Egyptians״ — every shepherd who sustains himself from the sheep and eats them, for it is their idolatry, well-known from the language of ״הרעה אותי,״ which is translated דזן יתי."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:12.248790510Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}